/// \class SpecialPowerModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1021_special_power_factories_more
/// \brief Base module data of the special-power modules: the shared
///        special-power table listed on the group page.
///
/// Most special-power data classes here start their field list from
/// SpecialPowerModuleData::buildFieldParse (group page, "Field tables").
/// The class is also the whole module data of the \c SpecialPowerModule
/// and \c SpecialPowerTimerRefreshSpecialPower module names, whose
/// registrations name SpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData. One
/// instance exists per module line per template, shared by every object
/// of the template.

/// \fn ModuleData *SpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for both "SpecialPowerModule" and
///        "SpecialPowerTimerRefreshSpecialPower": creates the base
///        special-power module data and parses the shared table into it.
///
/// It allocates the data, runs the SpecialPowerModuleData constructor and,
/// when \p ini is not null, calls INI::initFromINIMultiProc with
/// SpecialPowerModuleData::buildFieldParse, the special-power table listed
/// on the group page. A block under either name therefore accepts exactly
/// that table.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data, as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI


